# 4. SHARED ATTENDANCE DATABASE

Manual and QR attendance must use ONE underlying attendance system.

Create appropriate additive SQLite tables and indexes.

## Attendance Sessions

Store:

- Unique session ID.
- Faculty creator ID.
- Branch ID.
- Section ID or normalized section value.
- Date.
- Subject or period name.
- Optional period number.
- Start time.
- End time.
- Attendance method: MANUAL or QR.
- Status: DRAFT, ACTIVE, CLOSED, SUBMITTED as appropriate.
- QR duration and refresh interval.
- QR session start and expiration timestamps.
- Created and updated timestamps.

## Attendance Entries

Store:

- Session ID.
- Existing student account ID.
- Status: PRESENT, ABSENT, UNMARKED.
- Source: MANUAL, QR, CORRECTION.
- Recorded and updated timestamps.

Enforce one attendance entry per student per session.

## Correction Audit

Record:

- Session.
- Student.
- Previous status.
- New status.
- Editor account ID.
- Timestamp.
- Correction source.
- Optional reason.

Reuse existing audit infrastructure when appropriate.

For each session, create an attendance roster snapshot containing the approved students eligible when the session was created.

Do not dynamically add newly registered students to old sessions.

Never identify a student solely by the shortened class roll number in the database.

Use existing student IDs and official roll numbers.

Use transactions for bulk updates and corrections.

