For the initial release, campus-level location verification is sufficient.

Classroom-level tracking is NOT mandatory.

Do not spend time implementing advanced indoor positioning, Wi-Fi fingerprinting, Bluetooth beacons, or complex anti-spoofing systems.

Target institution:

Gayatri Vidya Parishad Institute of Higher Learning and Research, North Campus, Kommadi, Visakhapatnam, Andhra Pradesh.

The campus may also appear under older GVP institutional names.

Do not confuse different GVP campuses.

Do not invent precise campus coordinates.

## 8.1 Founder Geofence Configuration

Provide a simple Founder-only geofence settings page.

Founder can configure:

- Campus name.
- Verified latitude.
- Verified longitude.
- Allowed radius in meters.
- Whether GPS enforcement is enabled.

Store settings server-side.

Only Founder may modify them.

If coordinates are unavailable, clearly indicate that configuration is incomplete.

Do not pretend GPS is active when no valid campus boundary has been configured.

## 8.2 GPS Validation

For QR attendance:

- Request browser geolocation.
- Prefer high-accuracy positioning.
- Send coordinates, reported accuracy, and timestamp to the backend.
- Calculate distance to configured campus boundary server-side.
- Apply a reasonable configurable accuracy tolerance.
- Reject clearly out-of-bound locations.
- Reject stale or extremely inaccurate readings.
- Handle permission denial and timeouts clearly.
- Avoid continuous background tracking.
- Avoid unnecessary storage of raw coordinates.

Students located anywhere within the configured college premises may be accepted.

Do not require classroom-level accuracy.

GPS is an additional verification layer, not proof of classroom presence.

## 8.3 Temporary Demo Mode

Because the project has an immediate deadline, provide an explicitly controlled testing mode if GPS setup is incomplete.

Demo Mode must:

- Be Founder-only.
- Be disabled by default.
- Clearly indicate GPS enforcement is OFF.
- Never activate automatically.
- Preserve authentication, branch/section checks, QR expiry, and duplicate prevention.
- Be visibly distinguishable from real GPS-verified attendance.
- Be easy for Founder to disable.

Do not silently bypass GPS.

For students with camera or GPS problems, the faculty member may correct attendance manually.

Students must not be able to bypass GPS checks themselves.

