Prevent:

- Duplicate attendance entries.
- Expired QR reuse.
- Forged QR tokens.
- Cross-section attendance.
- Session ID manipulation.
- Unauthorized attendance editing.
- Student impersonation.
- SQL injection.
- XSS through editable fields.
- Unauthorized geofence changes.
- Accidental duplicate sessions.

Use server-side validation, database constraints, transactions, and existing security middleware.

Do not expose QR signing secrets or credentials.

Rate-limit sensitive endpoints without preventing normal classroom usage.

